## Getting started

```bash
npm install
npm run dev
```

This starts both apps at once:

| App      | Framework          | URL                                 |
| -------- | ------------------- | ------------------------------------ |
| Frontend | {{frontendLabel}} | {{frontendUrl}}                     |
| Backend  | {{backendLabel}}  | http://localhost:{{backendPort}}    |

Run them separately with `npm run dev:web` / `npm run dev:api` if you'd rather see their output in separate terminals.

## Project structure

```
{{projectName}}/
  apps/
    web/                # {{frontendLabel}} frontend
    api/                # {{backendLabel}} backend
  shared/
    design-tokens/      # framework-neutral colors, spacing, typography (CSS vars + JSON)
    contracts/          # openapi.yaml — the API contract both backends implement
  .env.example
```

`shared/design-tokens` and `shared/contracts` are the canonical, framework-neutral copies. The frontend app also keeps its own working copy of the tokens under `apps/web/src/styles` so its bundler doesn't need to reach outside its project root — treat the scaffolding templates as the source of truth rather than editing the two independently long-term.

